WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:04.003
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Billie Eilish.

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:05.404
And I --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.404 --> 00:00:06.706
I do want to
ask about "SNL,"

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:09.709
but congratulations on your
Oscar nomination.

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:12.178
-Oh, my gosh!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.546
-For your Bond song.
-I know.

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:16.115
And even being asked to do '
a James Bond song --

00:00:16.115 --> 00:00:17.450
it's such a unique thing.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.453
There's no other kind of
theme song where, you know,

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:22.121
through the years,
it's all these iconic musicians

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:23.489
have taken it on.

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:26.626
What was that process like
when you got asked to do it?

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:30.797
Like, who did you have to
meet with in the writing?

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:35.801
-Well, it was -- We made
the song in October of 2019.

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:37.070
So this was
a long, long time ago.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.772
-Yeah, that's a long time.
-It's a long time ago.

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:39.772
-That was a movie that got --
Okay.

00:00:39.772 --> 00:00:42.575
-So, 17 when we made it.
I'm now 20.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:43.542
-Yeah, there you go.
-Interesting.

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:46.713
-Yeah.
-Very, very weird.

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:51.150
Yeah, it was a, like, very long
kind of strategic process.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:53.252
It wasn't like,
"You got the job, here it is."

00:00:53.252 --> 00:00:56.489
We were auditioning,
pretty much.

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:59.025
So it was it was not,
like, an ego thing.

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:00.826
It was like, really,
it's got to be perfect.

00:01:00.826 --> 00:01:02.195
We've got to do it right.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:04.297
They weren't like, "Oh, yeah,
we want Billie Eilish."

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:07.733
It was like, "We want you,"
and we auditioned

00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:11.571
and kind of just, like, did our
best and worked really hard.

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:15.141
And it was a lot of, like,
Barbara, and she kind of gave us

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:17.210
the first little bit of
the script,

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:18.677
like, just, like, the opening,

00:01:18.677 --> 00:01:20.413
just so that we had a little,
like, taste of the movie.

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:22.715
-Was that helpful
in the writing of the song?

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.217
-It was literally
what wrote the song.

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:26.486
-That's wonderful.
-Yeah. It was great.

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:28.254
-And you got to meet with
Daniel Craig.

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:29.422
-Yeah.
-Were you nervous when you --

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:30.690
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:33.326
-Yeah. It's James Bond.
-Yeah, he's James Bond.

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:35.261
-He's James Bond.
-And --

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:36.329
-He's a DILF.

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:37.963
-He is a DILF.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.963 --> 00:01:39.265
Thank you for saying it.

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:44.236
I found, when I say it,
it's weird,

00:01:44.236 --> 00:01:47.106
but I want you to know that
I am in full agreement with you.

00:01:47.106 --> 00:01:48.174
-You should be.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:49.542
-But I didn't say it.
I just agreed.

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:50.977
-Those eyes? Girl...
-Yeah.

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:54.146
I mean, those eyes are crazy.
Look, let me just say something.

00:01:54.146 --> 00:01:55.915
You have a beautiful blue eyes.
I have beautiful blue eyes.

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.350
-You do. You absolutely do.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:01.353
-But we can't even be in the
same room as that man's eyes.

00:02:01.353 --> 00:02:02.655
-No, no, no, no. No.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:05.991
-These look like pinkeye
compared to him.

00:02:05.991 --> 00:02:07.626
-Literally,
you would not believe them.

00:02:07.626 --> 00:02:10.496
Like, they look crazy.
-They are crazy.

00:02:10.496 --> 00:02:12.231
-When I met him,
I was like, "Whoa!"

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:15.001
Like, they're, like -- It feels
like they're here on him.

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.268
Like, this is his face,
and these are his eyes.

00:02:16.268 --> 00:02:18.704
-Exactly.
Like, he's -- You want --

00:02:18.704 --> 00:02:20.573
If you weren't psyched about it,
you'd say,

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:21.808
"Your eyes are
in my personal space."

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.643
-Yeah, yeah, you would!

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.678
-The first time he looked at me,
I went, "DILF!"

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.846
I didn't --
couldn't stop myself.

00:02:28.914 --> 00:02:31.251
-You should get on that.
-Well, I don't know.

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:32.652
-Explore.
-I don't know.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.386
I do feel like it would be
weird if my wife said,

00:02:34.386 --> 00:02:36.155
"You get one hall pass,"
and I was like, "Daniel Craig."

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:37.723
-I don't think it
would be weird.

00:02:37.723 --> 00:02:38.858
I think you should do it.

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:40.392
-Thank you.
-Do you have a hall pass?

00:02:40.392 --> 00:02:41.461
-No.

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:42.961
-Daniel Craig.
-What? Yeah, no.

00:02:42.961 --> 00:02:46.399
Well, I'm going to have to go
talk to her about it.

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:49.501
You did a wonderful --
You and Finneas

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:50.603
are going to go
to the Oscars together.

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:51.804
-Yeah.
-That's really cool.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:52.805
-Yeah.

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:55.842
-Is there anything in particular

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:57.176
you're most excited about
the night?

00:02:57.176 --> 00:02:58.211
Will you be nervous
the whole day, being a nominee?

00:02:58.211 --> 00:02:59.979
-Oh, my God,
it's the scariest thing.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:02.048
No, I went to
the Oscars in 2020,

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:03.749
right before COVID happened,
and it was, like,

00:03:03.749 --> 00:03:06.085
the coolest,
scariest thing I'd ever --

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:07.987
I've never been more nervous
in my life.

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:10.122
"SNL" and the Oscars are, like,

00:03:10.122 --> 00:03:11.991
the scariest thing
I've ever experienced.

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:14.694
And -- 'Cause it's not people
that I know, really.

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:15.694
It's actors.

00:03:15.694 --> 00:03:17.530
And, also, actors are so

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.365
much more eloquent
than musicians.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.533
Like, musicians are, like,
weird and gross and smelly,

00:03:21.533 --> 00:03:25.104
and actors are, like, on time
and very -- I don't know.

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.572
So it was intimidating.

00:03:26.572 --> 00:03:28.608
I was --
Yeah, so I'm very nervous.

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:31.544
-If it goes anywhere
as well as your "SNL,"

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:32.612
you have nothing to worry about.

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.213
This was --
A lot of things I loved.

00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:37.550
This was my personal favorite.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:38.985
You and Kate
did this sketch together.

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:40.253
-Yeah.

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:42.989
-And this is very good
still photo, because it --

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:45.824
You never fully broke,
but it did seem like

00:03:45.824 --> 00:03:48.127
that was Kate's goal.

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:50.463
-Yeah.
We had trouble with this one.

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:51.964
We -- Yeah.

00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:56.569
Well, you know, in the dress
rehearsal, I was tearing up.

00:03:56.569 --> 00:04:01.774
I was dying laughing and I felt
like I was going to explode.

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:03.943
It was really
honestly genuinely painful.

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.510
Like, you know when
you're not supposed to laugh

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:06.612
and you have to laugh?

00:04:06.612 --> 00:04:08.147
It's -- It hurts.
It genuinely hurts.

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:09.749
-Also, watching it
and knowing the show,

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:10.983
there was no release point.

00:04:10.983 --> 00:04:12.918
You guys were on camera
the whole time.

00:04:12.918 --> 00:04:14.420
There wasn't a time where it
cut away where you could, like,

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:15.421
put yourself back together.

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:16.422
-I know.

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:19.558
And she just was
doing so many things

00:04:19.558 --> 00:04:21.527
that were pushing me
over the edge.

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:22.928
Oh, my God, it was infuriating.

00:04:22.928 --> 00:04:25.398
-And your your brother had
a fantastic cameo

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:26.465
in the sketch, as well.

00:04:26.465 --> 00:04:27.566
-Yeah.
-Now, was he --

00:04:27.566 --> 00:04:29.035
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah, it is.

00:04:29.035 --> 00:04:31.971
-Is he a hard sell on that
when they asked him to do it

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:33.539
or was he immediately like,
"I'm in"?

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:34.974
-Oh, he was in for sure.
-Yeah. He was great.

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:36.975
-It's "SNL"!
-Yeah, exactly.

00:04:36.975 --> 00:04:39.078
-Want a cameo, you get a cameo.

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:42.115
-I want to finish by asking --
Tell everybody what this is.

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:44.349
[ Cheers and applause ]
They seem to know.

00:04:44.349 --> 00:04:46.118
They seem to know.
-Okay.

00:04:46.118 --> 00:04:49.555
-So, this is my fragrance.

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:54.827
It's called Eilish,
and it's just --

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:56.495
It speaks for itself.
-Yeah, it does speak for itself.

00:04:56.495 --> 00:04:58.064
-It is -- Here.

00:04:58.064 --> 00:05:00.433
-Oh, look at that. Beautiful.

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:03.402
And, now, I heard that,
historically,

00:05:03.402 --> 00:05:06.538
your connection to the world of
fragrance, of perfume --

00:05:06.538 --> 00:05:08.174
this was something
you shared with your father.

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:09.775
-Yes.
-And how were you introduced?

00:05:09.775 --> 00:05:12.511
Did he take you to the fanciest
perfume shop in the land?

00:05:12.511 --> 00:05:15.714
-Macy's.
Yeah, he took me to Macy's.

00:05:15.714 --> 00:05:18.817
Yeah, fragrance and, honestly,
just, like, scent

00:05:18.817 --> 00:05:22.288
besides actual fragrances
has been, like, my biggest --

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:24.256
like, one of my --
the biggest parts of my life,

00:05:24.256 --> 00:05:26.459
if that even makes sense.

00:05:26.459 --> 00:05:28.961
I have what I used to call
a super-sniffer.

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:30.462
You guys watch "Psyche"
when you were little?

00:05:30.462 --> 00:05:33.633
Because I love that show.
-I watched it when I was little.

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:35.668
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:42.174
-I want to know --

00:05:42.174 --> 00:05:43.876
-Did you ever watch
"Welcome Back, Kotter"?

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:47.113
-No.
-Yeah, I thought.

00:05:49.081 --> 00:05:53.553
-No, but I've always had
a severe connection to scent,

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:55.120
and I remember
everything through scents

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:57.924
and people and colors
and all this crazy stuff.

00:05:57.924 --> 00:06:02.094
And, like, before I even had
any sort of a career

00:06:02.094 --> 00:06:05.097
or the idea of a career,
fragrance was, like,

00:06:05.097 --> 00:06:06.499
the most important thing
in my life,

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:08.701
and it, still to this day,
has been.

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:13.105
And I honestly am,
like, using this, like, facade

00:06:13.105 --> 00:06:14.573
that I've created of
Billie Eilish

00:06:14.573 --> 00:06:15.741
to promote a fragrance.

00:06:15.741 --> 00:06:18.043
Like, I'm, like --
I'm using my own clout.

00:06:18.043 --> 00:06:21.847
-Well, I think everything
you're using your clout for

00:06:21.847 --> 00:06:22.982
is making things better,
not worse.

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:24.116
And thank you so much
for being here.

00:06:24.116 --> 00:06:25.618
It was such a delight.
-I'm so honored!

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:27.053
-You guys, that's Billie Eilish.

